From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:54:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] leds: flash: lm3644: the Pixel 6 uses it too

The Pixel 6 Pro's rear flash LED is an LM3644TT on I2C 7, driven by the
same torch-only driver as the Pixel 7's. Say so in the help text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/leds/flash/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/flash/Kconfig b/drivers/leds/flash/Kconfig
index 875109b96..da3c972ca 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/flash/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/leds/flash/Kconfig
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ config LEDS_LM3644
 	help
 	  This option enables torch mode of the TI LM3644 and LM3644TT
 	  dual-channel flash LED drivers as an LED class device, as used
-	  for the rear flash LED of Google Pixel 7 phones.
+	  for the rear flash LED of Google Pixel 6 and 7 phones.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called leds-lm3644.
